{
  "info": {
    "name": "CareerVeda API — Security Tests",
    "description": "Attacker's-eye checks for the CareerVeda API, grouped by OWASP Top 10 (2021).\nEvery request is an attack; every test asserts the defence held. Green = protected.\n\nRUN ONLY AGAINST YOUR OWN DEPLOYMENT. Recommended: a staging copy.\n\nVariables (collection → Variables tab, or an environment):\n  baseUrl        API origin, e.g. https://careerveda.in (no trailing slash)\n  adminEmail     an admin account (super-admin or admin)\n  adminPassword  mark as type \"secret\"\n  totp           6-digit code if this admin has two-factor on; fill just before running\n  isProduction   \"true\" when testing the real https deployment\n  expectCaptcha  \"true\" when TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is set on the server\n\nRun the whole collection top to bottom with the Collection Runner (order matters:\n\"0 · Setup\" logs in first, \"A07\" ends by deliberately burning the session).\nThe \"⚠ Rate limits\" folder trips the login limiter for YOUR IP for 15 minutes — run it\nseparately, on staging, when you are not about to need the admin panel.\n\nWrites: none succeed on a protected server. If an XSS test FAILS it has created a\ndraft faculty record — delete it from the admin panel.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "",
      "type": "secret"
    },
    {
      "key": "totp",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "isProduction",
      "value": "false"
    },
    {
      "key": "expectCaptcha",
      "value": "false"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "csrfToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "rotatedRefresh",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "unknownLoginError",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Setup",
      "description": "Signs in so the authenticated attacks have a real, valid token to tamper with.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign in as admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const code = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"totp\");",
                  "pm.variables.set(\"totpField\", code ? `, \"totp\": \"${code}\"` : \"\");"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.error && body.error.code === \"MFA_REQUIRED\") {",
                  "  throw new Error(\"This admin has two-factor on: put a fresh code in the 'totp' variable and re-run.\");",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"signed in\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", body.data.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"csrfToken\", body.data.csrfToken);",
                  "const refresh = pm.cookies.get(\"cv_refresh\");",
                  "if (refresh) pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", refresh);",
                  "pm.test(\"response carries no password hash or 2FA secret\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.match(/passwordHash|argon2|totpSecret/);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"refresh cookie is HttpOnly and scoped to /api/v1/auth\", () => {",
                  "  const raw = pm.response.headers.filter((h) => h.key.toLowerCase() === \"set-cookie\").map((h) => h.value).find((v) => v.startsWith(\"cv_refresh=\"));",
                  "  pm.expect(raw, \"cv_refresh cookie\").to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "  pm.expect(raw).to.match(/HttpOnly/i);",
                  "  pm.expect(raw).to.match(/Path=\\/api\\/v1\\/auth/i);",
                  "  if (pm.collectionVariables.get(\"baseUrl\").startsWith(\"https://\")) pm.expect(raw).to.match(/;\\s*Secure/i);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\", \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"{{totpField}}}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
